{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED exact clean pushed head ddb18f38009944bdbe67d8010c9711d0224e761f, co-signing the docs artifact 1a5521a0, which is the only path this head changes. I ran every gate myself in a detached worktree at this exact head rather than repeating codex's report of them.\n\nARCHITECTURE. The only affected layer is the documentation set in docs/. No Go package, adapter, kernel, fold, storage or CLI surface is touched: the diff against main a45c166b is one commit, nine files, 9 insertions and 9 deletions, and every changed line is a rests_on front-matter entry. No layer contract in docs/reference/architecture.md changes, so that page correctly stays untouched and no candidate artifact is owed there. The head is based on current main, not stacked on the query-selector lane, which is what makes this diff reviewable in isolation.\n\nSECURITY. No trust or authority boundary is crossed. A rests_on entry is a provenance assertion about which artifact governs a page; it confers no capability, reads no untrusted input, and cannot widen authority. The one security-relevant property is that the successor must actually be live, because repointing at a second retired artifact would silently reproduce the defect under a different id. I checked it at review time rather than trusting the request text: 94cadf30 is live at path internal/nexus, not retired and not describes_superseded_world, and it survived the a45c166b merge untouched because that merge changed cmd/gs, docs, internal/statusview, cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/service, not internal/nexus. I also confirmed bc5ca55f no longer appears anywhere in the tree, in Go source as well as Markdown, so the class is closed rather than reduced.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Nothing to cut. Nine one-line substitutions, no prose churn, no reformatting, and no opportunistic repointing of the other retired citations that these same files carry, which is what the request asked for and is the right call: those need per-page decision